  "source_law": {
    "source": "NRS 484B.560(7)(a); with 484B.560(8)",
    "text": "It is unlawful for the driver of any vehicle: When crossing at grade any track or tracks of a railroad, to fail to completely cross the track or tracks without stopping due to insufficient: (1) Space for the vehicle on the opposite side of the railroad crossing; or (2) Undercarriage clearance of the vehicle. As used in this section, \u201ccompletely cross\u201d means to travel across a railroad track or tracks in such a manner that the trailing end of the vehicle is 15 feet or more past the nearest rail of the railroad track or tracks.",
    "sha256": "05c9b0823793d39cc18cda9ff91c2bb887599d2304a29c0773bd297a73685fd0"
  },
